Ours (dsv41 recipe), Apache-2.0, against vLLM main 6e517b15 + patches 0001-0021 + 0023-0025 (0023-0025 touch none
of its files, so 0001-0021 alone take it too).
The DSpark drafter's own lm_head, opt-in (VLLM_DSPARK_OWN_HEAD=1). V4.1's drafter shares the target's lm_head module,
so an EXL3 head is read twice a verify round, by the target's verify forward and by the draft forward: a K6 head
(~248 MB a rank at TP=2) costs ~1.0 ms a round over K4 at every depth. The drafter only proposes tokens, and its other
compression (experts K3, dense K5) cost no acceptance, so the target keeps its K6 head for quality and the drafter reads
a lighter encode of the same matrix (expected ~0.35-0.5 ms a round with a K4 drafter head on a K6 build).
With the flag, DSparkDeepseekV4ForCausalLM builds its head under the prefix "mtp_head" with the drafter's quant config.
If the config gives that prefix a method (the recipe's vllm_exl3_moe plugin: Exl3HeadMethod at exl3_moe.drafter_head_k,
which scripts/quantize/p4_drafter_head_variant.py writes next to the mtp.head.* tensors), the drafter keeps it
(keeps_own_lm_head: load_dspark_model skips the aliasing, whose _should_share would compare a .weight an EXL3 head does
not have), and load_weights fills it from mtp.head.{trellis,suh,svh,mul1|mcg} through the method's loaders, refusing to
start when a declared piece is missing. Without the flag the drafter builds today's placeholder and shares the target's
head, byte for byte as before; with it but no method for the prefix (no drafter head in the checkpoint) it warns and
does the same. mtp.head.* tensors are skipped whenever the head is shared (the target's weight mapper already drops
every mtp.* name). The own head has the placeholder's geometry (vocab 129,280, padding 64, the TP group), so each rank
holds the target head's vocab columns: _vocab_shard, the local draft argmax (0012) and the Markov cache rows (0011) read
the same columns. Verification is untouched: greedy rounds accept against the target's own argmax and sampled rounds use
the distribution the drafter sampled from, so outputs keep the target's distribution and only acceptance can move.
Memory: +~165 MB a rank for a K4 drafter head. Test: patches/tests/test_dspark_own_head.py (CPU, in the serve image).

